      "spam": false,
      "value": "not to sound troll-ish, but a search engine and 30 seconds of time got me to this:\nIt looks like it kind of already sort of does... if you use something like this \n\nhttp://www.osvr.org/getting-started.html\n\nThe HDK Windows Installer is an all-in-one package that installs everything you need to get your HDK ready to play. This includes files needed to run native and SteamVR games.\n\nwhich would lead one to believe if it's able to be used for SteamVR, it should be able to be used for VRChat\nthough I could be wrong, I hope not as the price point for the open source stuff is almost 1/4 that of a vive, and would help bring some more \"competition\" into the VR ring.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
